Four NAK fixes from Mesa main that are in no Mesa release yet (26.3.0 does not have them). Upstream text (MIT licence),
unchanged, oldest first:
  commit 61f3a1d0 nak: use correct src_type for OpBSSy bar_in
  commit 77781ae8 nak: fix insert order when annotate is off
  commit 3b3084bf nak: Derive copy and clone in lat_rs_gen
  commit 83a732aa nak: Increase sm120 imma/hmma latencies
The first two are for every generation with barrier registers: the barrier input of BSSy was typed as a predicate, and
with annotations off the copy of a barrier phi into a GPR was inserted before the phi it reads.
The last one is for RTX 50 (SM120) only: more cycles between the matrix multiply-accumulate instructions (IMMA, HMMA)
and the readers and writers of their registers, from latencies measured on the hardware; the third is the derive it
needs.

